{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960761,"nonce":"tVF51BJnKGzZXEhUS1OoPecGL8o=","title":"the native backend cannot run on iOS","message":"native.rs drives winit with `EventLoopExtPumpEvents::pump_app_events`, which winit provides on Windows, macOS, X11, Wayland and Android. iOS has only `run_app`, which never returns, so `poll` and `wait` cannot pump there and the backend does not compile for iOS targets. cb_window has the same limit.\n\nRunning on iOS needs a backend that runs the loop itself and hands the program its turns, such as from a host that already owns the main loop.","files":null}]}